            <ArticleTitle>Successful operation on a coronary arteriovenous fistula in a 74 year old woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>107-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary arteriovenous fistulas are rare and are usually diagnosed in children or young adults. Most are believed to be congenital. A right coronary arteriovenous fistula was first diagnosed in a patient of 74. Despite her age the fistula was successfully operated on and her symptoms were relieved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
